###############################################################
############### ANGULAR ENTERPRISE ARCHITECTURE ################
###############################################################

# OBJECTIVE

Build a production-grade Angular application.

This is NOT a CRUD application.

This is an Enterprise Healthcare Platform.

Every architectural decision must prioritize:

Maintainability

Scalability

Performance

Readability

Reusability

Accessibility

Long-term development

------------------------------------------------------------

# ANGULAR VERSION

Use the latest stable Angular version supported by the project.

Use ONLY modern Angular APIs.

Never use deprecated APIs.

------------------------------------------------------------

# STANDALONE

Use Standalone Components ONLY.

Do not create NgModules unless absolutely required by a third-party library.

Application bootstrap must use:

bootstrapApplication()

ApplicationConfig

provideRouter()

provideHttpClient()

Functional Providers

------------------------------------------------------------

# APPLICATION STRUCTURE

Organize the project using Feature-Based Architecture.

Never organize by component type.

Correct:

features/
    auth/
    dashboard/
    patients/
    assessments/
    sessions/
    exercises/
    reports/
    chatbot/
    profile/
    settings/

Wrong:

components/

pages/

services/

misc/

------------------------------------------------------------

# ROOT STRUCTURE

src/

app/

core/

layout/

shared/

features/

assets/

environments/

styles/

------------------------------------------------------------

# CORE LAYER

Core contains ONLY global application logic.

Core may include

Authentication

Guards

Interceptors

Global Services

API Configuration

Error Handler

Application Configuration

Environment

Tokens

Storage Services

Logger

Never place feature-specific logic inside Core.

------------------------------------------------------------

# SHARED LAYER

Shared contains reusable UI.

Examples

Buttons

Cards

Dialogs

Inputs

Dropdowns

Tables

Badges

Icons

Avatar

Charts

Pipes

Directives

Validators

Utility Components

Shared must NEVER depend on Features.

------------------------------------------------------------

# FEATURE STRUCTURE

Each Feature must have

feature/

pages/

components/

dialogs/

services/

models/

interfaces/

routes/

state/

guards/

pipes/

utils/

------------------------------------------------------------

# ROUTING

Every feature must use Lazy Loading.

Use loadComponent()

or

loadChildren()

where appropriate.

Never place all routes inside app.routes.ts.

------------------------------------------------------------

# ROUTE ORGANIZATION

Routes must follow

Authentication

↓

Main Layout

↓

Feature

↓

Child Pages

↓

Dialogs

↓

Fallback

------------------------------------------------------------

# ROUTE GUARDS

Use

Authentication Guard

Authorization Guard

Guest Guard

Unsaved Changes Guard

Role Guard

Permission Guard

Never duplicate guard logic.

------------------------------------------------------------

# LAYOUT SYSTEM

Create reusable layouts.

Public Layout

Authentication Layout

Dashboard Layout

Admin Layout (if needed)

Never duplicate navigation.

------------------------------------------------------------

# STATE MANAGEMENT

Prefer Signals.

Use computed()

Use signal()

Use effect()

Use RxJS ONLY for

HTTP

Streams

SignalR

Complex async flows

Avoid BehaviorSubject unless necessary.

------------------------------------------------------------

# DATA FLOW

Backend

↓

API Service

↓

Repository (optional)

↓

State

↓

Component

Never access HttpClient directly inside Components.

------------------------------------------------------------

# API LAYER

Every Feature has

Models

Interfaces

Services

Mapping

Validation

Error Handling

Loading State

------------------------------------------------------------

# COMPONENT DESIGN

Components must be

Small

Focused

Reusable

Typed

Stateless whenever possible

Presentation components should not contain business logic.

------------------------------------------------------------

# SMART COMPONENTS

Smart Components

Handle

API

Navigation

State

Dialogs

Notifications

------------------------------------------------------------

# DUMB COMPONENTS

Receive Inputs

Emit Outputs

No HTTP

No Business Logic

No Routing

------------------------------------------------------------

# FORMS

Use Typed Reactive Forms ONLY.

Never use Template Driven Forms.

Forms must support

Validation

Async Validation

Dynamic Validation

Error Messages

RTL

Accessibility

------------------------------------------------------------

# VALIDATION

Validation Rules come ONLY from Backend.

Do not invent validation.

Do not duplicate inconsistent validation.

------------------------------------------------------------

# TABLES

Create reusable data table.

Support

Pagination

Sorting

Filtering

Searching

Selection

Bulk Actions

Export

Loading

Empty State

Responsive

------------------------------------------------------------

# DIALOGS

Reusable dialog framework.

Support

Confirmation

Delete

Warning

Error

Success

Edit

Create

Preview

------------------------------------------------------------

# ERROR HANDLING

Every HTTP call must support

Loading

Retry

Unauthorized

Forbidden

Validation Errors

Network Failure

Unexpected Error

------------------------------------------------------------

# INTERCEPTORS

Authentication

Refresh Token

Error Handling

Loading Indicator

Request Correlation

Never duplicate interceptor logic.

------------------------------------------------------------

# FILE UPLOAD

Create reusable upload component.

Support

Drag & Drop

Progress

Cancel

Retry

Validation

Preview

Multiple Files

------------------------------------------------------------

# SIGNALR

Create reusable SignalR service.

Support

Reconnect

Auto Retry

Connection Status

Notifications

Real-Time Chat

------------------------------------------------------------

# PERFORMANCE

Use

OnPush

Signals

trackBy

Lazy Loading

Deferrable Views

Image Optimization

Route Preloading (where beneficial)

Avoid unnecessary subscriptions.

------------------------------------------------------------

# ACCESSIBILITY

Every page must support

Keyboard Navigation

Focus Management

Screen Readers

ARIA Labels

Color Contrast

High Contrast Mode

------------------------------------------------------------

# RTL

RTL must be native.

Never hack RTL with CSS overrides.

Support both

Arabic

English

if localization exists.

------------------------------------------------------------

# RESPONSIVENESS

Desktop

Laptop

Tablet

Mobile

Large Mobile

Small Mobile

No horizontal scrolling.

------------------------------------------------------------

# STYLING

No inline styles.

No duplicated CSS.

Use Design Tokens.

Use CSS Variables.

Use reusable utility classes where appropriate.

------------------------------------------------------------

# CODE STYLE

Strict TypeScript

Strict Templates

No any

No console.log

No dead code

No commented code

No duplicate logic

------------------------------------------------------------

# BUILD RULE

Every architectural decision must preserve:

Clean Architecture

Feature Isolation

Scalability

Performance

Maintainability

